      <div class="acc"><details>
            <summary>Will it purge or break out more at first?</summary>
            <div class="acc__body"><p>Purging is not typically expected with this serum. The serum has been clinically tested on 36 women, and it no reported dryness, irritation or newer breakouts. However, individual skin can respond differently. If you notice an initial purging or increase in breakouts-it’s not usually a bad reaction, but your skin adjusting to the serum. Think of it as flushing out the accumulated toxins before starting fresh. In such a case, give your skin some time to adjust and keep monitoring how it responds with time.&nbsp;</p></div>
          </details><details>
            <summary>Can I use it with my current routine?</summary>
            <div class="acc__body"><p>Yes. It replaces your treatment step. Keep a gentle cleanser, a moisturiser and sunscreen. Avoid layering other strong acids or retinoids alongside it.</p></div>
          </details><details>
            <summary>How long before I see a difference?</summary>
            <div class="acc__body"><p>Skin renews on a cycle. Real change needs about two of them. That is why the 30 + 30ml pack exists.</p></div>
          </details><details>
            <summary>Is it suitable for sensitive skin?</summary>
            <div class="acc__body"><p>The serum is designed to be well tolerated by sensitive skin, but we recommend patch test first before using. If you experience any discomfort, discontinue use.</p></div>
          </details><details>
            <summary>can I use LNGVTY Serum on active acne?</summary>
            <div class="acc__body"><p>Yes. The formulation is designed to decongest pores, one of the primary reasons for having an acne &amp; to calm the inflammation.&nbsp;</p></div>
          </details><details>
            <summary>Do I need a pigmentation serum on top of this to fade post-acne marks?</summary>
            <div class="acc__body"><p>You can but you don’t need to. This serum is designed to work beyond active acne. Niacinamide, Glycolic Acid and Lactic Acid help improve the appearance of post-acne marks, while Salicylic Acid helps clear the pores. Give the serum time to work on both concerns rather than adding another treatment layer.</p></div>
